    {
      "id": "claim_80c165723d094986bff45bde70e5e214",
      "statement": "The answer-code wire format is sdpEncode(localAnswerSdp) + '|' + publicKeyBase64 (key empty when the receiver downgraded to plaintext — a valid, intentional artifact); the offer peer's acceptAnswer first refuses to signal a dead peer (PR #104): if the channel's onerror/onclose handler already ran (or a racing regeneration closed the peer), it checks !connection || connection.connectionState === 'closed' and toasts 'Connection lost — generate a new offer to connect' instead of reaching setRemoteDescription on a closed peer, which would only fail with a misleading 'Invalid answer code'; it then parses the code with parseAnswerCode, which splits on the LAST '|', distinguishes a missing separator from a well-formed empty-key code (which follows the receiver into plaintext via effectiveEncrypt=false instead of dead-ending the handshake), and on a missing separator or damaged non-empty key toasts 'Invalid encryption key in answer code' and aborts before setRemoteDescription; a key present in the code pins the session to encrypted; the SDP decode + setRemoteDescription runs inside its own try/catch that toasts 'Invalid answer code' on malformed SDP (PR #45); the receive page likewise decodes the user-controllable s param and calls setRemoteDescription inside a try/catch that toasts 'Invalid SDP in link' instead of crashing the page during load (PR #45).",
