    {
      "id": "claim_5b41d4320b424ab8ab56a4606ddf1ead",
      "statement": "The offer peer creates the data channel (ordered:false) and the answer peer receives it via ondatachannel; both pin dataChannel.binaryType = 'arraybuffer' at channel acquisition (offer at the createDataChannel site, answer at ondatachannel) before the onopen wiring, because WebRTC's default 'blob' would make new Uint8Array(Blob) zero-length and Message.decode silently drop every frame (guaranteed no-op transfer, PR #95); both install the same handlePeerMessage handler from src/utils/peerMessage.ts (deduplicated from two identical per-page handlers, PR #71) with Message.decode on peer-controlled bytes guarded by try/catch (toast + drop the frame instead of an uncaught crash, PR #46) and unlock the Send/Receive transfer UI on channel open. Both pages additionally wire the channel's onerror/onclose to sender?.onChannelClose()/receiver?.onChannelClose() so a dead channel propagates the connection-lost state into the file pipelines (PR #74; the onChannelClose bodies and the guarded send() now live in the shared src/utils/channelSender.ts helper, PR #97), and both onerror and onclose additionally call connection.close() guarded on connectionState !== 'closed' (PR #104): closing the data channel alone does not close the RTCPeerConnection — its ICE agent, UDP sockets, and STUN/TURN keepalives would stay live for the rest of the page's lifetime; the guard prevents InvalidStateError from an error-then-close double-fire or a racing regeneration. Pinned by tests/peer-message-handler.test.mjs (including a static guard asserting binaryType = 'arraybuffer' exactly once per page at the acquisition site), tests/channel-sender.test.mjs, and tests/dead-channel-peer-close.test.mjs (static guard: each page's dataChannel.onclose and onerror handler contains a guarded connection.close(), OfferPage.acceptAnswer bails before setRemoteDescription when the peer is missing or closed, and the offer page now carries four guarded connection.close() sites in total — two death handlers + regeneration teardown + the PR #108 offer-creation catch).",
