      "id": "claim_0353b2cee9c84ee0aef157512da079a9",
      "statement": "ICE configuration is resolved through the shared isSupportedIceServer predicate (built-in STUN allowlist — including stuns: for the TLS-served nextcloud relay — plus any well-formed stun/stuns/turn/turns URL) on BOTH sides: the offer page resolves its RTCPeerConnection iceServers and the emitted 'i' link param through resolveIceServer, and the receive page accepts 'i' only when it passes the same predicate, falling back to the default with an error toast otherwise — so a custom/TURN server chosen on the sender is always honored by the receiver and no asymmetric ICE configuration can break NAT traversal or TURN relaying.",
