    {
      "id": "claim_a18f75c58d0648e6b3879e26bff57b82",
      "statement": "Failure handling: a missing or empty 's' param on the receive page redirects to origin and throws; ICE candidate errors, data channel errors, and close events toast an error, clear isConnecting, and blank the offer link on the offer side to prevent reuse of a stale link; onerror and onclose additionally call sender?.onChannelClose()/receiver?.onChannelClose() so in-flight/queued files on both sides exit with an accurate 'connection lost' error instead of dead-ending or re-firing false per-chunk errors (PR #74; the onChannelClose bodies and the guarded send() now live in the shared src/utils/channelSender.ts helper, PR #97), and both onerror and onclose additionally call guarded connection.close() to release the RTCPeerConnection itself (PR #104 — closing the data channel alone leaves the ICE agent, UDP sockets, and STUN/TURN keepalives live; the guard prevents InvalidStateError from an error-then-close double-fire or a racing regeneration); offer-generation failures (synchronous constructor throws or rejected createOffer/setLocalDescription) toast 'Could not generate the offer', re-enable the button, and — since PR #108 — tear down the just-created generation with the same guarded shape as the regeneration teardown (clear the pending ICE-candidate timer, null the four data-channel handlers before dataChannel.close(), and close the just-created RTCPeerConnection guarded on connectionState !== 'closed'), so a failed generation cannot leak its ICE agent/UDP sockets/STUN keepalives or let late-firing channel handlers stomp the current generation's UI (pinned by tests/offer-processing-failure.test.mjs); and on the receive side an unappliable offer sets offerFailed, which replaces the perpetual 'Generating Answer' spinner with an error state ('Could not connect: the offer in the link is invalid') instead of dead-ending the page (PR #49).",
