    {
      "id": "claim_bea7261033f04a9f892f9d10695a81be",
      "statement": "The Copy Link and Copy Answer buttons — the keyboard-free path of the link/code exchange — never dead-end the manual P2P handshake silently (PR #79): copyOfferLink and copyAnswerCode wrap navigator.clipboard.writeText in try/catch, so a rejection (SecurityError in a non-secure context, NotAllowedError on denied permission, DataError, or navigator.clipboard undefined in some webviews) toasts a 'Copy failed — select the … text and copy it manually' error instead of escaping as an unhandled rejection that would leave the user believing the link/answer code was copied when it was not.",
